WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.840
In 1961, a German Protestant dean told
an American rabbi that the Holocaust was

2
00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:07.750
part of God's will.

3
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:10.200
The rabbi was Richard Rubenstein.

4
00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:14.380
He could not accept it, and
later spoke of the death of God.

5
00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:17.370
In London, another rabbi
who had fled Germany,

6
00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:21.360
Ignaz Maybaum, read the same
events very differently.

7
00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:26.430
How could one say God had died, while
the other said God was still at work?

8
00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:29.820
In this mission, you'll follow
Rubenstein's chain of reasoning,

9
00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:31.570
one link at a time.

10
00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:35.570
Then you'll read the Bible passage Maybaum
used to explain the suffering of the

11
00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:36.980
six million.

12
00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:42.450
Your mission: explain how two rabbis
read the same catastrophe so differently.
